//
// Phase E4 operator gate: transpose.
//
// The bf16 matrix transpose iron's runlist dispatches as k_transpose,
// re-expressed over data_transfer_transpose/dma_bf16/'s movement pattern
// (contiguous tiles + a scalar tile kernel -- a DMA-stride transpose is not
// legal for sub-32-bit types) and tiled over an 8x1 herd. Validated at
// 4096x768, the k^T shape the gate configuration implies; the runlist mode's
// README records why the mode itself does not dispatch it (its consumer, the
// attention scores GEMM, is host torch on this device).
//
// Runs opcheck.py on real NPU2 against the exact transposed input: np.isclose
// over the full output at rtol=1.6e-2 with zero permitted mismatches, which
// for pure data movement means BIT-exact -- and it measures exactly that:
// every error statistic is 0.0. A nonzero anything here is a moved byte.
//
// NPU serialization lives one layer down, not in the recipe below. Device
// access is locked on /tmp/npu.lock, which XRTRunner.run_test holds across
// xclbin load and dispatch -- the same inode lit.cfg.py's NPU substitution and
// KernelCache take. Taking the outer /tmp/mlir-air-npu.lock here instead would
// DEADLOCK against the gate command that already holds it -- BSD flock(2)
// treats a second open() of the same file as a foreign lock.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for its directives, so naming
// one in prose -- even inside a comment -- registers as a second directive and
// leaves the test UNRESOLVED. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_transpose_peano
// RUN: cd test_npu2_transpose_peano
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-transpose PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// The exactness first -- every statistic zero, which no arithmetic operator in
// this example prints -- then the verdict naming the operator and shape.
// CHECK: [precision] Output 0 (3145728 elements): mean_rel_L1=0.000e+00 | rel_err max=0.000e+00 | abs_err max=0.000e+00
// CHECK: PASS!
// CHECK: [opcheck] transpose [4096x768]: PASS
